<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ragged Guard</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rongyos Gárda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ragged Guard was a Hungarian irregular paramilitary force active after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, made up largely of former officers, students and nationalist volunteers. In August 1921, when western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was due to be handed over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, its units attacked the Austrian gendarmes and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgenland">Burgenland</a>, and its leaders proclaimed the Banate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leitha">Leitha</a>. They withdrew after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice-protocol">Venice Protocol</a> of October 1921.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ragged-guard.jpg" alt="Ragged Guard" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ARongyosGardaSopronban(1921).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
